{"name":"Polished Marble","hex":"#d0bc9d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"polished","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made smooth or shiny by polishing.","Refined, elegant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of polish"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polished"},{"term":"marble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metamorphic rock of crystalline limestone. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A small ball used in games, originally of marble but now usually of glass or ceramic."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (something to have) the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example by mixing viscous ingredients incompletely, or by applying paint or other colorants unevenly.","To get or have the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example due to the incomplete mixing of viscous ingredients, or the uneven application of paint or other colorants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marble"}],"entries":[{"title":"Polishing","blocks":[{"text":"Polishing is the process of creating a smooth and shiny surface by rubbing it or by applying a chemical treatment, leaving a clean surface with a significant specular reflection. In some materials, polishing is also able to reduce diffuse reflection to minimal values."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polishing","wikidata":"Q1054722"},{"title":"Marble","blocks":[{"text":"Marble is a metamorphic rock consisting of carbonate minerals (most commonly calcite (CaCO3) or dolomite (CaMg(CO3)2) that have recrystallized under the influence of heat and pressure. It has a crystalline texture, and is typically not foliated (layered), although there are exceptions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Marmo_z17.JPG/330px-Marmo_z17.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marble","wikidata":"Q40861"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Marbleboot.jpg/500px-Marbleboot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Marbleboot.jpg/1280px-Marbleboot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Marbleboot.jpg/500px-Marbleboot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Marble Boat, a lakeside pavilion in the Summer Palace in Beijing, China","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarbleboot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Taj_Mahal_%28Edited%29.jpeg/500px-Taj_Mahal_%28Edited%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Taj_Mahal_%28Edited%29.jpeg/1280px-Taj_Mahal_%28Edited%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Taj_Mahal_%28Edited%29.jpeg/500px-Taj_Mahal_%28Edited%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Taj Mahal is clad entirely in marble","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaj_Mahal_(Edited).jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Catedraldemarmol.JPG/500px-Catedraldemarmol.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Catedraldemarmol.JPG/1280px-Catedraldemarmol.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Catedraldemarmol.JPG/500px-Catedraldemarmol.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Folded and weathered marble at General Carrera Lake, Chile","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatedraldemarmol.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Fossils_on_Marble_floor_tile.jpg/500px-Fossils_on_Marble_floor_tile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Fossils_on_Marble_floor_tile.jpg/1280px-Fossils_on_Marble_floor_tile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Fossils_on_Marble_floor_tile.jpg/500px-Fossils_on_Marble_floor_tile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fossils on Marble floor tile","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFossils_on_Marble_floor_tile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Ephesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg/500px-Ephesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Ephesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg/1280px-Ephesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Ephesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg/500px-Ephesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Library of Celsus in Ephesus, Turkey. Turkey is the largest marble exporter in the world.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEphesus_Celsus_Library_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Marble_wall_of_Ruskeala.jpg/500px-Marble_wall_of_Ruskeala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Marble_wall_of_Ruskeala.jp